WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.109
Pseudo-localization swaps your
source text for an accented,

2
00:00:04.109 --> 00:00:05.722
padded, bracketed version.

3
00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:08.890
Hardcoded strings, truncation,

4
00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:13.371
broken fonts, and concatenated
sentences show up before any

5
00:00:13.371 --> 00:00:14.752
translation exists.

6
00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:20.989
Android ships the en-XA and
ar-XB pseudo-locales for it.

7
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.587
General Translation lets you
test real translations during

8
00:00:24.587 --> 00:00:25.318
development.

9
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:30.911
With a project API key that has
runtime translation permission,

10
00:00:30.911 --> 00:00:33.940
gt-next requests
translations on demand.

11
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:38.264
For release, generate translations
with the CLI and review

12
00:00:38.264 --> 00:00:39.250
them in the running app.

13
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:42.331
Your team now ships
German with each release.
